.TH EZA-NVIM-LINKS 1 "2026-06-30" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eza-nvim-links \- run eza with Neovim-aware OSC-8 file links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eza-nvim-links
.RI [ eza-args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eza-nvim-links
wraps
.BR eza (1)
with
.B --hyperlink
and rewrites file hyperlinks when termnav knows the current remote host. This
lets terminal file links open in the correct local or remote Neovim context.
.PP
All arguments are passed through to
.BR eza .
When stdout is a terminal, the wrapper restores selected TTY-derived defaults
that
.B eza
would otherwise lose while output passes through the link-rewriting pipe.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_REMOTE_LINK_HOST
Remote host identity to embed in generated
.B file://
links.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_EZA_NVIM_LINKS_FORCE_TTY
Set to
.B 1
to exercise TTY presentation behavior in tests while stdout is piped.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.B eza
completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The context library could not be loaded.
.TP
.B 2
The wrapper could not resolve its installed library path.
.TP
.I other
The wrapper exits with the status returned by
.BR eza .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eza (1),
.BR nvim-link-host (1),
.BR nvim-tmux-open (1)
